{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, פִּתְגָם","hw":"פִּתְגָם","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">פִּתְגָם</span></big>  <strong>n.m.</strong> <sup><a data-ref=\"Ezra 6:11\" href=\"/Ezra.6.11\">Ezr 6:11</a></sup> <strong>command, word, affair (</strong>Pers.: v. BH<strong>)</strong>;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">פ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 3:16\" href=\"/Daniel.3.16\">Dn 3:16</a>; emph. -<span dir=\"rtl\">מָא</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:17\" href=\"/Ezra.4.17\">Ezr 4:17</a> +;—<em>command</em> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 6:11\" href=\"/Ezra.6.11\">Ezr 6:11</a>, <em>word</em>, by missive <a data-ref=\"Ezra 5:7\" href=\"/Ezra.5.7\">5:7</a>, from king <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:17\" href=\"/Ezra.4.17\">4:17</a> (both c. <span dir=\"rtl\">שְׁלַח</span>), in answer <a data-ref=\"Ezra 5:11\" href=\"/Ezra.5.11\">5:11</a> (c. <span dir=\"rtl\">התיב</span>); weakened, <em>thing, affair</em> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 3:16\" href=\"/Daniel.3.16\">Dn 3:16</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:14\" href=\"/Daniel.4.14\">4:14</a>.","next":"BDB Aramaic, פְּתַח","prev":"BDB Aramaic, פְּשַׁר²"}